  "label": "Secular humanist ideology",
  "description": "The meme aligns with secular humanist ideology, which emphasizes reason, science, and individual autonomy over religious belief. The claim that 'religion has to be taught' reflects the secular humanist view that belief systems are constructed through education and socialization, not innate or divine. This ideology is often used to critique religious institutions and promote secular education.",
